---
/**
 * /privacy-policy
 *
 * 🔴 INDEXED URL — rewritten IN PLACE at exactly this path (scope §2 decision 11
 * and §8). A redirect here would cost a ranked page for no benefit.
 *
 * Grounded in the research in website-scope.md §1:
 *   - Originally a RingCentral vendor template with ~12 blank company-name
 *     fields. Read literally, sections named no company at all.
 *   - RingCentral is named throughout WITH its rate limits (50/60/180 msgs/min).
 *     ✅ CONFIRMED: the agency is migrating to RingCentral, so naming it is
 *     correct and the template's detail turns out to describe the destination.
 *     This does not lock anything — it documents a decision already made.
 *   - The SMS consent framework (STOP/UNSUBSCRIBE, proof of consent with
 *     timestamps, double opt-in) is genuinely solid and is retained.
 *
 * ⚠️ ONE THING TO CHECK BEFORE LAUNCH: the live DNS zone for insure-big.com
 * carries a Twilio domain-verification TXT record (`_twilio`), and AgencyZoom
 * lists Twilio as an available telephony integration. If Twilio is also in use,
 * this section should name both platforms rather than RingCentral alone.
 *
 * ⚠️ NOT LEGAL ADVICE. Drafted by a technologist from the agency's own policy and
 * public filings. Bret must have it reviewed before launch (scope §8).
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE, LOCATIONS, CONTACT } from '../config/site.js';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema.js';

const path = '/privacy-policy';
const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', path },
];

const effectiveDate = '2026-01-01';

const schema = [
  webPageSchema({
    path,
    title: `Privacy Policy — ${SITE.name}`,
    description: `How ${SITE.name} collects, uses, shares and protects personal information, including SMS/MMS messaging consent and your rights.`,
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(trail),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | BIG"
  description="How Ballentine Insurance Group collects, uses and protects your personal information, including SMS messaging consent, opt-out rights and data retention."
  path={path}
  schema={schema}
>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />

  <article class="container-page py-12">
    <div class="prose-page">
      <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
        <strong>Effective date:</strong> {effectiveDate}<br />
        <strong>Last reviewed:</strong> {effectiveDate}
      </p>

      <h2>1. Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to {SITE.name}. We are dedicated to protecting your privacy and ensuring
        that your personal information is handled in a safe and responsible manner. This
        Privacy Policy outlines the types of information we collect from you when you
        visit the website at <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>
        {' '}(the "Website") or use the services provided through it (the "Service"). It
        also describes how we use, share, and protect your information, and the choices
        you have.
      </p>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} uses RingCentral as its business telephone and messaging platform.
        References in this policy to SMS/MMS messaging, message consent, opt-out
        handling, and messaging rates describe that platform. See section 6.
      </p>
      <p>
        This policy is designed to comply with applicable data protection laws and
        regulations, including relevant federal law and the laws of the States of
        Missouri and Kansas, together with applicable telecommunication privacy
        standards.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy applies to all individuals and entities who interact with the
        Website and the Service, regardless of their location. It encompasses the
        collection, use, and disclosure of personal information by {SITE.name} and its
        affiliates. This policy covers information collected through our Website, mobile
        applications, SMS/MMS communications, and any other electronic means of
        interaction.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where additional or separate privacy notices are presented to you in the course
        of an interaction, those notices will apply in conjunction with this policy to the
        extent of any inconsistencies.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Consent</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing or using the Website and the Service, you consent to the collection,
        use, disclosure, and processing of your personal information as described in this
        Privacy Policy. This consent applies to all information practices carried out by
        {' '}{SITE.name}.
      </p>
      <p>
        When collecting personal information — particularly for activities that involve
        telephony services such as SMS/MMS messaging — we adhere to stringent consent
        requirements. Explicit, informed, and unambiguous consent is obtained from all
        individuals prior to the collection of their personal data. This includes clear
        and conspicuous opt-in mechanisms for marketing communications and any
        telecommunication activities, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards set
        forth by bodies such as the Federal Communications Commission, the Telephone
        Consumer Protection Act (TCPA), the Cellular Telecommunications Industry
        Association (CTIA), and applicable state law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may require your express written consent in certain circumstances,
        particularly for automated messaging campaigns and any data-sharing activities
        that fall under strict regulatory frameworks. You may withdraw your consent at any
        time, subject to legal or contractual restrictions and reasonable notice, by
        contacting us using the details in section 14.
      </p>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes
        in our practices, legal requirements, and regulatory obligations. Your continued
        use of the Website and the Service constitutes your acceptance of any
        modifications. Notice of any significant updates will be provided through a
        prominent notice on our Website or through direct communication channels.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>
          Phone numbers provided for SMS opt-in will remain confidential and will not be
          shared with any third parties.
        </strong>
      </p>

      <h2>4. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        {' '}{SITE.name} is committed to transparency concerning the information we collect
        about you.
      </p>

      <h3>Personal information</h3>
      <p>
        We collect personal information that can be used to identify you as an individual,
        collected either directly from you or through your interactions with our services.
        This includes, but is not limited to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Name</strong> — full legal name</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact details</strong> — email address, postal address, telephone number,
          and other similar contact information
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because we are an insurance agency, we may also collect information necessary to
        quote or place coverage — for example property details, vehicle details, and
        coverage history. That information is used for underwriting and is shared with
        carriers only as required to obtain a quote or administer a policy.
      </p>

      <h3>Billing information</h3>
      <p>
        For transactional and billing purposes we may collect financial information
        including payment card number, expiration date and security code, and the postal
        address associated with the payment method. This information is stored in
        compliance with the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS).
      </p>

      <h3>Usage information</h3>
      <p>
        To optimise and enhance your experience, we gather usage data reflecting your
        interactions with our services and Website, including IP address, service usage
        data, calling history (records of calls made and received, including timestamps
        and durations), and click patterns on the Website.
      </p>

      <h3>Anonymous information</h3>
      <p>
        We also collect anonymised data that cannot be used to identify you personally,
        compiled from multiple users in a manner that ensures individual anonymity. The
        purpose of collecting anonymous data is to conduct market research, improve our
        services, monitor performance, and support commercial activities without
        compromising individual privacy.
      </p>

      <h3>Additional information</h3>
      <p>
        In the course of providing our services we may also collect supplementary
        information necessary for business operations, including business name and related
        details for commercial clients, demographic details, technology preferences, and
        referral information (how you discovered {SITE.name}).
      </p>

      <h2>5. How we use your information</h2>
      <p>
        {' '}{SITE.name} is committed to ensuring that the information we collect is used
        in a manner that is transparent, secure, and compliant with applicable laws and
        regulations.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Regulating access</strong> — authenticating your identity, controlling
          access to services, and implementing security measures to protect against
          unauthorised access and breaches.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Personalisation</strong> — tailoring content and service offerings based
          on your interests and previous interactions, and personalising interfaces to
          improve usability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Promotions and marketing</strong> — sending you promotional materials
          related to our products and services through email, SMS, and other channels,
          subject to obtaining your prior consent where required by law; and using usage
          data and preferences to design and target effective campaigns.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Customer contact</strong> — service notifications about important
          updates, changes or issues; customer support; and surveys and feedback.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Internal and administrative purposes</strong> — data analysis, audits and
          compliance, and risk management.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Billing and support</strong> — transaction processing, account
          management, and technical support.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal compliance</strong> — disclosing information to comply with legal
          obligations, court orders, or official requests from law enforcement agencies;
          meeting industry regulations, telecommunication laws, and data protection
          legislation; and enforcing our user agreements.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. SMS/MMS messaging</h2>
      <p>
        {' '}{SITE.name} takes compliance with SMS/MMS regulations and guidelines
        seriously. This section outlines the policies and procedures governing our use of
        SMS and MMS messaging, which we operate on the RingCentral platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        Phone numbers provided for SMS opt-in remain confidential and are not shared with
        any third parties.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Written consent requirements.</strong> For any marketing, promotional or
          informational messaging, we obtain explicit written consent from recipients
          before sending messages. This consent is documented and maintained to
          demonstrate compliance with the TCPA and CTIA guidelines.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Express and logged consent.</strong> Automated SMS messaging requires
          express and logged consent from the recipient — clear and documented approval to
          receive automated messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Opt-out requirements.</strong> Every automated message includes clear
          opt-out instructions (for example, "Reply STOP to end"). All opt-out requests are
          processed immediately so recipients can easily discontinue receiving messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Double opt-in.</strong> We recommend and may use a double opt-in process
          to confirm consent and validate contact information. This involves sending a
          confirmation message to which the recipient must respond affirmatively.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consent tracking.</strong> Detailed records of consent are maintained,
          including timestamps and methods of opt-in, to provide proof of consent if
          requested by carriers or regulatory bodies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Message frequency and rates.</strong> Message frequency varies with your
          interaction with us. Message and data rates may apply depending on your mobile
          carrier and plan.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Messaging rates and platform terms.</strong> Our use of messaging
          services is governed by RingCentral's Terms of Service and Acceptable Use
          Policy, which exist to prevent spam, phishing and fraudulent messaging. To
          maintain the integrity of the service and comply with carrier policy, we limit
          the number of messages sent per originating number. Non-compliance with carrier
          rules can result in reduced deliverability, suspension, or the passing through of
          carrier penalties.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Opt-out procedures</h3>
      <p>
        Opt-out instructions are clearly communicated in all informational, marketing or
        promotional messages. Recognised keywords such as <strong>STOP</strong> and
        {' '}<strong>UNSUBSCRIBE</strong> are honoured immediately. Where our messaging
        platform manages opt-outs automatically we rely on that; where messages are sent
        from numbers outside such a solution, opt-out requests are managed manually. We
        ensure opt-out requests received through any channel are processed to prevent
        further messaging to those recipients.
      </p>

      <h3>Prohibited campaigns and content</h3>
      <p>
        We do not send, and will not accept instructions to send, messages concerning loan
        or mortgage advertisements, credit repair or debt relief offers, debt collection,
        work-from-home or secret shopper advertisements, political messages, alcohol,
        tobacco or firearms advertisements, pharmaceutical or drug advertisements, illegal
        activities, pornographic or adult content, violent or hateful content, references
        to controlled substances, or fraudulent and deceptive content.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Information storage and security</h2>
      <p>
        {' '}{SITE.name} is committed to safeguarding the integrity, confidentiality and
        availability of your personal information.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Physical safeguards</strong> — access to physical storage locations is
          restricted to authorised personnel, with secure locks and access verification.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Electronic safeguards</strong> — personal information is stored on
          secure, encrypted servers, protected by firewalls, intrusion detection and
          prevention systems. Regularly scheduled backups support recovery in the event of
          accidental loss or hardware failure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Managerial safeguards</strong> — access is granted on a need-to-know
          basis and reviewed regularly, and personnel handling your data are trained on
          data protection practices.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Encryption</strong> — data at rest is encrypted using industry-standard
          protocols such as AES-256, and data in transit is protected using Transport
          Layer Security (TLS).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Secure access controls</strong> — multi-factor authentication is required
          for accessing sensitive systems, and we conduct regular security audits and
          vulnerability assessments.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Data retention</h3>
      <p>
        We retain your personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes
        for which it was collected, or as required by applicable laws and regulations.
        Retention periods are guided by business and operational needs, and by legal and
        regulatory requirements — which for insurance records can be a number of years
        after a policy ends. When personal information is no longer required, it is
        securely deleted using industry-standard methods, or anonymised where ongoing
        analysis is required.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Data sharing and disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>
          Phone numbers provided for SMS opt-in will remain confidential and will not be
          shared with any third parties.
        </strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        We may disclose your personal information where required to comply with any
        applicable law, regulation, legal process or governmental request; to protect the
        rights, property or safety of {SITE.name}, our users, employees or the public; or
        to enforce our terms of service and respond to claims or litigation involving
        {' '}{SITE.name}. Where we disclose, we take reasonable steps to limit the scope of
        disclosure to what is required and to ensure appropriate protections are in place.
      </p>
      <p>
        As an insurance agency, we share information with insurance carriers and
        intermediaries strictly as needed to obtain quotes, place coverage, and administer
        claims and renewals on your behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to provide a user-friendly and
        efficient browsing experience.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Essential cookies</strong> — required for the operation of our Website
          and services, including security, network management and accessibility.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Performance cookies</strong> — collect anonymised information about how
          visitors interact with our Website, used solely to improve performance and
          usability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Functionality cookies</strong> — remember choices you make, such as
          language preferences, to provide a more personalised experience.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Targeting/advertising cookies</strong> — used, with your consent, to
          deliver relevant advertisements and assess campaign effectiveness.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also use web beacons to understand whether emails are opened and to track
        on-site behaviour, and log files which capture IP addresses, browser type and
        version, internet service provider, referring and exit pages, timestamps, and
        clickstream data. You can control cookies through your browser settings; disabling
        essential cookies may affect how the Website functions.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your rights and choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Access and update</strong> — you may request a copy of the personal
          information we hold about you, and request corrections or updates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Marketing opt-out</strong> — you may opt out of marketing communications
          at any time using the unsubscribe link in any marketing email, or by contacting
          us directly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SMS opt-out</strong> — reply <strong>STOP</strong> or
          {' '}<strong>UNSUBSCRIBE</strong> to any message, or contact our support team to
          manage your messaging preferences.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deletion</strong> — you may request deletion of your personal
          information. We will review each request and act in compliance with applicable
          law. Note that we may be required to retain certain records to meet insurance
          regulatory obligations, and residual copies may persist in backup archives for a
          period.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our Website and services are directed at adults. We do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children under 13. If you believe we have, please
        contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Our Website may link to third-party sites, including insurance carriers and
        quoting tools such as our form provider. We are not responsible for the privacy
        practices of those sites, and we encourage you to read their policies.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The effective date at the top
        of this page will change when we do, and material changes will be notified through
        a prominent notice on our Website or by direct communication.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact information</h2>
      <p>
        For any question about this policy, to exercise any of the rights described above,
        or to make a complaint about how we have handled your information, contact us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>By email:</strong>
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>By phone:</strong> <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref}>{CONTACT.phone}</a>,
          {' '}{CONTACT.hours.display}
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>By post:</strong> {SITE.name}, {LOCATIONS[0].full}
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you may also contact the Missouri
        Attorney General's Office or the Kansas Attorney General's Office, depending on
        where you reside.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
